  "invert_match_requirement": "Pair-matched or common-mode invert scale is invisible (R1/R2 preserved). The binding invert-resistor relationship is the ratio: systematic R2/R1 error of 0.075% is at the analog bar (signed; -0.075% MAE=1.10e-3 fails, +0.075% MAE=8.81e-4 passes). Independent unmatched invert resistors: 0.075% mean-passes (8/8); 0.15% mean-passes but worst-draw fails (5/8); 0.5% mean-fails. Limited MC, not a yield.",
  "candidate_text": "Ranked: (1) keep VCVS baseline; (2) XSPICE `limit` invert (LEVEL 2, \u00b115 V, documented ngspice code model); (3) teaching miller invert (LEVEL 4, Exp 26 CMOS-OP1 W/L, \u00b12.5 V); (4) miller + invert servo (Exp 28 invert_dw=0.0026, 27 \u00b0C self-balance, not per-input); (5) OPA1656 invert (LEVEL 3, \u00b115 V, include not copy); (6) stimulus polarity copies for input/Vref only (system interface); (7) passive grounded divider (negative control). No foundry invert cell is installed.",
  "passive_text": "A resistor network to analog ground cannot implement Vout = \u2212Vin. KCL at a grounded tap only produces a positive attenuation. Tying the invert mid node to 0 without an amp forces Vout \u2192 0 through R2. Differential subtraction still needs a physical difference primitive. Charge-domain inversion is a sampled switch/C method (Exp 27 CDS family), not a DC substitute for the 32 hidden inverts on this OP fabric. The isolated passive bench is the measurement. Stimulus polarity copies are allowed only for Vin/Vref because those nodes are already ideal sources.",
  "temp_text": "No fabric resistor TCR is documented. Default ngspice R has none; none was invented. MOS `.temp` on the teaching miller invert is a device-temperature test of the *amp*, not of Rf\u00b7G. IHP / SkyWater are not installed. r2_cmc usable=False: Note: No compatibility mode selected!\n\n\nCircuit: r2_cmc\n\n\nError on line 4 or its substitute:\n  nrr2_cmc 1 0 rmodel w=1u l=20u isnoisy=1\nUnable to find definition of model rmodel\n    Simulation interrupted due to error!\n\nError: incomplete or empty netlist\n       or no \".plot\", \".print\", or \".fourier\" lines in batch mode;\nno simulations run!. Temperature of Architecture A ratios therefore remains unvalidated.",
